{"t": 44.251, "n": 59, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The preview passed (14 checked). I made no file edits this visit, so there was nothing new to commit. All four verification commands came back `reused`, with 0 run, from results recorded for this same tree.\n\n- **Rule files:** I opened `task-notes.rule.md` and `plan.rule.md` with the read tool.\n- **Plan state:** `status` is `completed` and every row in phases 1 to 7 carries a mark. The report lists the earlier deviations, including the extra `\"proves\": \"EVS-AC7\"` key in the five fixtures and the third reason-line pin in `test_regeneration_run.py`.\n- **Specs read:** I read these specs against the code:\n  - `regeneration.spec.md`\n  - `regeneration-failures.spec.md`\n  - HUM-B15 to B18 and HUM-AC11 to AC13 in `gate-and-human.spec.md`\n  - SCF-B24, SCF-B25, SCF-AC9 and SCF-AC10 in `blueprint-and-scaffold.spec.md`\n- **Engine code read:**\n  - `validate.py` gives the four refusal codes and `back-on-map`.\n  - `nodes.py` writes the BACK verdict only for a judge-less `on_fail: back` gate with at least one failing finding and exactly one target. An environmental failure still escalates, and a failure with no finding still retries.\n  - `gate.py` builds the numbered reason lines, and the loop-budget test still applies.\n  - `registry.other_checkout` and the `verify.py` register rung pass for another checkout and still refuse a different package with `name-taken`.\n- **Test bodies read:** I read `test_gate_back.py`, the `HUM-AC13` test, the `SCF-AC9` and `SCF-AC10` tests, and all of `test_regeneration.py`. Each asserts what its criterion states, so the tests would fail if the result were absent. I did not open the other test files this visit.\n- **Contradictions found:** None.\n- **Rule-12 comparison with `regeneration.py`:** The module matches RGN-B3 to B12 and B16, and RGF-B1 to B4 and B8. The check names `ts-rgn-declaration`, `ts-rgn-ran` or `ts-rgn-passed` in every result.\n- **Left for the operator:** `plugins/temperspec-tgraph/stamp.json`, `authoring.json` and `diagram/` still need refreshing with `tempergraph author verify plugins/temperspec-tgraph`. No row edits them by hand, as the plan says.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: docs/tasks/i203a.report.md\nARTIFACT tests_passed: yes", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "00f58cee-bdb5-4204-812b-c70223100027"}
